{%- comment -%}
  Size guide, opened inline under the Size picker on the PDP.

  Usage: {% render 'size-guide', rows: section.settings.size_rows, heading: ..., note: ..., summary: ... %}

  A <details> disclosure rather than a modal, deliberately: it needs no
  JavaScript, so it still opens with scripts off, and the browser gives the
  expanded/collapsed state to a screen reader for free. A <dialog> would need
  showModal() and therefore a working script just to be readable.

  Rows come from one textarea setting, pipe-separated, first line the header:

    Age | Height | Chest (in) | Length (in)
    4-5 Y | 104-110 cm | 12.5 | 17

  A textarea rather than blocks because a size chart is one table that changes
  as a whole. Blocks would put eight rows in the theme editor's block list
  alongside the badge blocks main-product already has, and reordering a size
  chart by drag is worse than editing eight lines of text.

  Every number here is a general Indian kidswear standard, not a measurement
  taken off a JJW garment — the note setting says so on the page, and it must
  keep saying so until real numbers replace these.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lines = rows | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
  comment
    `if line | strip != blank` fails the push with "Expected end_of_string but
    found pipe" — an if condition takes a value, never a filter chain, exactly
    as a render argument does. Assign first.
  endcomment
  assign line_count = 0
  for line in lines
    assign probe = line | strip
    if probe != blank
      assign line_count = line_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if line_count > 1 -%}
  <details class="sg">
    <summary class="sg__toggle accent-caps">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M2 6h16v8H2z" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M6 6v3M10 6v4M14 6v3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
      {{ summary | default: 'Size guide' | escape }}
    </summary>

    <div class="sg__panel">
      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <p class="sg__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        tabindex + role make the scrollable table reachable and announced; a
        region that scrolls but takes no focus cannot be panned by keyboard.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sg__scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="{{ summary | default: 'Size guide' | escape }}">
        <table class="sg__table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {%- assign header_cells = lines.first | strip | split: '|' -%}
              {%- for cell in header_cells -%}
                <th scope="col">{{ cell | strip | escape }}</th>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
          {%- for line in lines -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign trimmed = line | strip
              if trimmed == blank
                continue
              endif
              assign cells = trimmed | split: '|'
            -%}
            {%- unless forloop.first -%}
              <tr>
                {%- for cell in cells -%}
                  {%- if forloop.first -%}
                    <th scope="row">{{ cell | strip | escape }}</th>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <td>{{ cell | strip | escape }}</td>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </tr>
            {%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {%- if note != blank -%}
        <div class="sg__note">{{ note }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
